What is an Articulated Truck Gearbox?
Articulated truck gearboxes are robust power‑train components that translate engine output into precise, low‑speed torque required for heavy‑load haulage. Typically integrated as powershift or fully automatic units, they combine a torque converter with planetary gear sets to deliver seamless acceleration, rapid gear changes, and resilience against frequent start‑stop cycles on rugged terrain. Pricing for these gearboxes varies between $30,000 and $120,000 per unit, with the majority of mainstream models positioned in the $50,000‑$100,000 range.
